{"notation": "Each case runs one instruction on one wave. ins is the instruction at the decoded level , the machine's input, which bypasses any.s reader: {op (canonical name), kind, operands, fields}, each operand {reg: [file, first, count]} or {lit: [32-bit pattern, text]} (lane-mask vcc as [vcc, 0, 2] at W = 64, count W / 32; the cases run at W = 32), as in reading.json. line spells it for reading only (canonical name and operands v<n>, s<n>; informative, not a.s syntax). Lane l holds lane (l mod 4)'s values and tags, 4 lanes shown. A tag is '-' (none), 'mB:O' (a memory tag: buffer B, byte offset O; '+hi' marks the high-nibble flag), or ['sum', x, y] (a sum record of the two sources x and y in order). tags_in/tags_out give each register's 4 byte tags per lane, byte 0 first. values: each vector register's 4 lanes, and each scalar register (s<n>) its one dword, the same in every lane; any other register holds the poison value. exec, when given, is the active-lane mask of lanes 0..3, repeated every 4 lanes. vcc holds the poison value 0x7fc17fc1. No GEMM checker or scale table is present.", "cases": [{"line": "v.mov.b32 v1, v8", "ins": {"op": "v.mov.b32", "kind": "valu", "operands": [{"reg": ["v", 1, 1]}, {"reg": ["v", 8, 1]}]}, "values": {"v8": ["0x3f80beef", "0x12345678", "0x00ff00ff", "0xffffffff"]}, "tags_in": {"v8": [["m0:0", "m0:1", "m0:2", "m0:3"], ["m0:4", "m0:5", "m0:6", "m0:7"], ["m0:8", "m0:9", "m0:10", "m0:11"], ["m0:12", "m0:13", "m0:14", "m0:15"]]}, "tags_out": {"v1": [["m0:0", "m0:1", "m0:2", "m0:3"], ["m0:4", "m0:5", "m0:6", "m0:7"], ["m0:8", "m0:9", "m0:10", "m0:11"], ["m0:12", "m0:13", "m0:14", "m0:15"]]}, "values_out": {"v1": ["0x3f80beef", "0x12345678", "0x00ff00ff", "0xffffffff"]}}, {"line": "v.mov.b32 v1, v8", "ins": {"op": "v.mov.b32", "kind": "valu", "operands": [{"reg": ["v", 1, 1]}, {"reg": ["v", 8, 1]}]}, "values": {"v8": ["0x3f80beef", "0x12345678", "0x00ff00ff", "0xffffffff"], "v1": ["0x00000000", "0x00000000", "0x00000000", "0x00000000"]}